# Known problem (probe-rs fork c18738d, TriCore): once the core runs on from an instruction
# breakpoint (which steps over it first), a data breakpoint no longer halts it. This script
# shows it: it ends with exit code 2 at line 19 until that is fixed.
#
# The flash demo (start_in_flash): compute() writes g_result before it returns, so from the
# breakpoint at its first line (38) the next stop is the data breakpoint.

attach ../../dap-client/examples/tc275_demo_3cores.json
continue all
pause 0
wait stopped 0
watch g_result write
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason data breakpoint within 3s
break ${AURIX_DEMO:-C:/work/aurix_tcf_demo}/src/demo.c:38
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason breakpoint within 3s
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason data breakpoint within 3s
